# series charon: patch -p1 in charon/ of the upstream source
#
# charon: compact span encoding by default, interned in deduplicated files
#
# Spans took a quarter of large LLBC files ({"data":{"file_id":..,"beg":{"line":..,"col":..},
# "end":{..}},"generated_from_span":..}). A span is now the array [file, beg_line, beg_col,
# end_line, end_col], followed by five more numbers when generated_from_span is present. This
# replaces the CHARON_COMPACT_SPANS prototype: the compact form is the only one.
#
# When values are deduplicated (the default; not with --no-dedup-serialized-ast), spans are also
# interned like hash-consed values: the first occurrence of each distinct span is prefixed with its
# id (6 or 11 numbers), later ones are the id alone. Ids are consecutive in serialization order and
# the deserializers check that, so a decoder that skips a span fails instead of shifting ids. Spans
# in stateless positions (ItemMeta) are written without id.
#
# generate-ml decodes spans with a hand-written span_numbers_of_json (span table in of_json_ctx),
# and also decodes opaque fields that may contain spans (they must be visited in order, like
# hash-consed values).

